{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792594601,"nonce":"IWik4t7VSG4dUjuHWnr0McBUMMo=","message":"Landed in 21f3e451ffba22605f3bea998ed64da2339f5e41.\n\nProfile: one hybrid offscreen run per condition, 1280x800, 58 tabs (Main plus 57 generated 100-field/100-method files), packaged Rayzor SHA-256 c8eb19fd537e134e2862a7d78f3609908613f99d271cbf0192a9626f99955c04. Rayzor sources and builds were not changed. Client and direct children were sampled separately using vmmap; the probe pauses while the sampler runs. GC totals describe allocation traffic and heap blocks, not RAM.\n\nBefore fixes, collected client physical footprint with 58 tabs was 409.8 MiB (off) versus 463.5 MiB (Rayzor). After all tabs closed and collection: 348.0 versus 349.9 MiB, with zero retained client documents, pending requests and active CodeEditor components. Rayzor child used 81.7 MiB at idle and 83.0 MiB after completions, separate from the client. The client retained 467769 document characters; these are references to editor text, not a mirror of Rayzor semantic caches. No accumulating client document cache was reproduced. Physical footprint varied between fresh runs and includes allocator/JIT/driver effects.\n\nIdle tick stress, 10000 calls with 58 synchronized documents: 46.7269 MiB allocated / 228.6 ms before, 3.5887 MiB / 10.4 ms after. The change skips scans of already synchronized documents and avoids empty event arrays. This is a 92.3% allocation-traffic reduction in the stress phase, not a RAM reduction or production poll frequency.\n\nDiagnostic ablation through the Workbench LSP callback (200 synthetic diagnostics, transport excluded): first hidden publication 47.9 -\u003e 20.2 MiB allocated; identical refresh 97.1 -\u003e 8.8 MiB. Before, 200 Problems rows existed hidden and after panel close. After, rows are 0 hidden / 200 shown / 0 closed. Collected heap blocks after a close were 86.1 -\u003e 69.6 MiB; physical footprint did not fall correspondingly (allocator high-water). Data and editor squiggles remain; only the hidden list view is released. Problems scroll offset survives remount.\n\nRemaining completion issue f3e9f8f: popup builds up to 200 rows for 10 visible rows and retains its last items/rows on hide. Five completion opens allocated 2880.7 MiB with Haxe fallback versus 339.9 MiB with Rayzor; this is whole-phase traffic, not an attribution of every byte to rows. Follow-up records virtualization and metadata-release work.\n\nRaw results: bin/lsp-memory-58-before/results.json, bin/lsp-memory-58-after/results.json, bin/lsp-diagnostics-before/results.json, bin/lsp-diagnostics-after/results.json and bin/lsp-memory-summary.json. The initial 11-tab exploratory run is superseded by the 58-tab run for closed-editor ownership (the probe local editor reference was cleared).\n\nValidation: scripts/check.sh passed, including unchanged diagnostics, changed message/range, documents opened after initialize, unchanged document versions under polling, incremental sync, cancellation, crash replay, manual stop/start/restart. Both diagnostic GPU probes passed, including scroll restoration. No PNG snapshots: visible layout is unchanged.\n\nBuild: native bin/rayde and bin/RayDE.app rebuilt successfully. Existing user changes in LanguageServers.hx and docs/languages.md were preserved and excluded. No new Cargo targets, worktrees, or Rayzor source/build changes.","files":null}]}